# WS6 Stage-C drill — C1 ESO machine-identity, RECREATE-FROM-ESCROW template.
# REC-PLAN-021. *** TEMPLATE ONLY — NO SECRET MATERIAL. NEVER committed with values. ***
#
# This documents the SHAPE the harness produces. The harness does NOT apply this file with
# values inlined; instead recreate_machine_identity_from_escrow() runs the imperative form so
# the value is PIPED and never lands in a manifest or a last-applied-configuration annotation:
#
#   set -a; . <(age -d -i "$ESCROW_IDENTITY" eso-bootstrap.age); set +a
#   kubectl -n external-secrets create secret generic infisical-machine-identity \
#       --save-config=false \
#       --from-literal=clientId="$INFISICAL_MI_CLIENT_ID" \
#       --from-literal=clientSecret="$INFISICAL_MI_CLIENT_SECRET"
#
# WHY C1: external-secrets/infisical-machine-identity (clientId/clientSecret, Universal Auth) is the
# ONE credential ESO uses to authenticate to Infisical — the thing that unlocks Infisical, so it
# cannot be synced FROM Infisical. In a cold start NOTHING in the cluster can recreate it; it must
# come from the OFFLINE escrow the founder holds (eso-bootstrap.age, opened by the offline age key).
# The drill asserting that the 5 ClusterSecretStores go Valid *because of* this proves the escrow is
# sufficient (C1). --save-config=false avoids re-leaking the values into an annotation (Stage-A finding).
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: infisical-machine-identity
  namespace: external-secrets
  labels:
    restormel.dev/escrow: "offline-age (eso-bootstrap.age)"
    restormel.dev/control: "C1"
    restormel.dev/throwaway: "true"
  annotations:
    restormel.dev/do-not-sync: "ESO bootstrap root — recreate from sealed offline escrow ONLY; apply with --save-config=false"
type: Opaque
# data: INTENTIONALLY OMITTED (clientId / clientSecret). Recreated from escrow at run time.
